  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q5_Connectivity
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Two PCs on the same subnet can ping each other but neither has a
    default gateway set. Is that a fault?
  choices:
  - "Yes \u2014 nothing works without a gateway"
  - "No \u2014 a gateway is only needed to reach other networks"
  - Yes, but only for the server
  - No, because the switch acts as the gateway
  correctChoiceIndex: 1
  points: 10
  explanation: Traffic inside one subnet is switched directly. The default gateway
    is the address a host sends traffic to when the destination is not on its own
    network.
